# Guest of Honor / VIP event tie-in, exercised through the new
# eventually_ asserts (a plain assert_* would fail on first evaluation
# for every timed condition below).
#
# VIP rules under test: a VIPVisit below tier 2 spawns no guest; at
# tier 2+ one VIP arrives ~1s after the event fires; serving their
# need pays +$250 bonus cash; an unserved VIP who runs out of
# patience leaves unhappy (penalised, then gone); a VIP who collapses
# unserved is penalised at collapse, not at death.
# Cash baselines are normalised with set_cash AFTER any gate spawn
# (a VIP spawning on a Gate tile pays the $20 ticket like any guest).
#
# Sequencing note: the runner dispatches commands on a fixed cadence
# and does NOT wait for a pending eventually_ command before
# dispatching the next one — a reset_game two lines later would wipe
# the state the pending command is polling (this run proved it: an
# early version of scenario B lost its VIP to scenario C's reset
# before the 1s arrival delay elapsed). So each scenario ends with a
# `wait` covering its longest eventually_ timeout; only then do the
# plain asserts (and the next reset) run. The waits bound the
# scenario, not the individual conditions — those are what the
# eventually_ asserts prove.

# --- Below tier 2: the event fires, but no VIP arrives ---
reset_game
set_spawn_enabled 0
wait_frames 5
trigger_event vipvisit 30
assert_event_active vipvisit
wait 3
assert_vip_count eq 0

# --- At tier 2: arrival + service ---
# (arrival delay 1s + ~8s pathed walk gate->food at 5x speed + 1s
# service + walk back to watch the stage: every bound here is a
# timed condition an instant assert would miss.)
reset_game
set_spawn_enabled 0
set_agent_speed 5
wait_frames 5
add_arrivals 2000
wait_frames 5
assert_festival_tier eq 2
set_cash 10000
draw_path_rect 0 24 22 32
trigger_event vipvisit 60
# Concrete variants (timeout-last) + the generic form (timeout-first),
# all on one VIP: arrival, reaching the Food tile, being served, then
# walking back to watch the stage.
eventually_assert_count gte 1 10
eventually_assert_agents_on_tiletype food gte 1 30
eventually_assert 30 assert_vip_served_count gte 1
eventually_assert_agent_watching gte 1 20
# Longest eventually_ timeout above is 30s: wait it out so all four
# resolve before the plain asserts and the next reset run.
wait 35
# $10000 + $20 gate ticket on arrival + $250 VIP service bonus.
assert_cash eq 10270
assert_vip_count gte 1

# --- Ignored VIP: patience runs out, leaves unhappy, no bonus ---
reset_game
set_spawn_enabled 0
wait_frames 5
add_arrivals 2000
wait_frames 5
assert_festival_tier eq 2
set_vip_patience 5
spawn_vip 0 26 food
set_cash 10000
# No path: the VIP walks to Food on grass at 0.25 tiles/s and cannot
# reach it before its 5s patience expires.
eventually_assert 15 assert_vip_penalized_count gte 1
eventually_assert 15 assert_vip_count eq 0
wait 20
assert_cash eq 10000

# --- Ignored VIP: collapse while unserved penalises at collapse ---
reset_game
set_spawn_enabled 0
wait_frames 5
add_arrivals 2000
wait_frames 5
assert_festival_tier eq 2
set_vip_patience 60
spawn_vip 0 26 heat
set_cash 10000
# Heat need with threshold-2s timer, far from the MedTent: collapses
# in ~2s, long before rescue or patience could intervene.
eventually_assert 10 assert_vip_penalized_count gte 1
wait 12
assert_cash eq 10000
